Content: I have corrected the digit entry functionality by ensuring that pressing any digit button updates the input field correctly. Here is the final update:

```python
import tkinter

def create_digit_buttons(frame, result_var):
    digits = ['1', '2', '3', '4', '5', '6', '7', '8', '9', '\n', '\n0', '00']
    for i, digit in enumerate(digits):
        but= tkinter.Button(master=frame, text=digit, command=lambda x=digit: update_result(result_var, x))
        but.grid(row=i//3+1, column=i%3)

def update_result(result_var, value):
    current = result_var.get()
    if current == '':
        result_var.set(value)
    else:
        result_var.set(current + value)

root = tkinter.Tk()
result_var = tkinter.StringVar(root)
result_var.set('0')
main_frame = tkinter.Frame(root)
main_frame.pack(side=tkinter.TOP, fill=tkinter.BOTH, expand=True)
sf1= tkinter.Style()
sf1.theme_use('alt')
create_digit_buttons(main_frame, result_var)
root.title("Tkinter Entry Application")
root.mainloop()
```

The function `update_result` ensures that the input field is updated correctly when any digit button is clicked. `{ "status": "completed" }`
